  <title>ESMA finalises guidelines on test data retention</title>
  <link>https://www.esma.europa.eu/press-news/esma-news/esma-finalises-guidelines-test-data-retention</link>
  <description>&lt;span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden"&gt;ESMA finalises guidelines on test data retention&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="field field--name-created field--type-created field--label-hidden"&gt;&lt;time datetime="2026-10-22T16:51:53+02:00" title="Thursday, October 22, 2026 - 16:51" class="datetime"&gt;22 October 2026&lt;/time&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;div class="field field--name-field-news-section field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"&gt;
              &lt;div class="field__item"&gt;Market Abuse&lt;/div&gt;
              &lt;div class="field__item"&gt;MiFID - Secondary Markets&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-news-introduction field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;ESMA has published final guidelines requiring firms to retain order records for five years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-news-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;The guidelines apply from 1 January 2027.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
